	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12268"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=317" title="View the profile of Vanden RN">Vanden RN</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 197<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=317"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1209.msg12268#msg12268"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1209.msg12268#msg12268">Re: So this board sees a ton of action</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #39 on:</b> October 31, 2004, 12:44:17 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Zorlo posted:<br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">But please, i have absolutley no doubt that my vocabulary is larger then yours by a magnitude you can&#039;t possibly comprehend. I tried not to use any words that you would deem too &quot;complex&quot; or whatever you we&#039;re getting at in your post, but seriously, while you have the proof to back up your points on my grammar mistakes, you have little to no idea of how comprehensive my vocabulary is.</div><br />I was not &quot;getting at&quot; anything... I was pointing out how inadequate you were at taking what you thought was the intellectual high road by putting others down for their vocabulary.  You found her posts annoying and saw an avenue to ridcule her.  It was therefore obvious that your intent was simply to put her down, not that her grammar is any worse than yours.  I could care less that it was mean, but it was funny to see someone who can&#039;t spell try and bash someone else for the same thing.<br /><br />Two of my minors were in philosophy, so I am pretty sure that I <i><span style="text-decoration: underline;">can</span> </i> comprehend the magnitude of your vocabulary if you were to show us.  <i>(Hey, at least I got something out of philosophy besides how to debate and see the big picture.  Unfortunately it crushed many of my beliefs on religion and similar things.  I&#039;m willing to bet some others on this board know what I mean...)</i><br />Here&#039;s a question for you:  does it count toward your vocabulary level if you can&#039;t actually spell the words or if you don&#039;t know in which context to use them?  <br /><br />Okay, back to the magnitude of your vocabulary skills.  I have two degrees, one of which is in the field of English (I wanted to be able to write columns... English and philosophy were going to be my roadmaps prior to polit-sci).  You make a personal jab that your vocabulary is larger than mine.  I do not know you, so what is there for me to dispute?  Based on your previous post samples, I believe my education in English and literature allows me to use my miniscule vocabulary to greater effect than you can use your vastly superior dictionary and thesaurus.  Assuming you are using one of those tools, you might want to read up on the difference between <span style="text-decoration: underline;">were</span> and <span style="text-decoration: underline;">we&#039;re</span>.<br /><br /><span style="text-decoration: underline;">My conclusion:</span><br />You speak two languages, English being your second.  I admire that, since I only speak English and an embarrassing amount of French and Spanish.  Combined, your vocabulary is vastly superior to mine.<br /><br /><span style="text-decoration: underline;">My suggestion:</span><br />If you are going to try and ridicule people for their spelling and grammar, please do so in your native language.  I&#039;m quite sure it will be easier to read, and less embarrassing to you.  A second benefit is that when someone else views the boards who also understands that language, they will obviously see what we cannot see... how precise and correct you were in blasting someone else&#039;s use of written language.<br /><br /><br />Zorlo, have you ever seen one lousy driver call someone else a lousy driver, and then say in defense &quot;well at least I only stall out, I don&#039;t grind the clutch...&quot;?
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
